WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.760
Microsoft OpenSource Agents, so 1,024 coding agents, can coordinate themselves on program bench without any central orchestrator. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 214. Memory written into weights, cognitions, vulnerability skills, and a week in review follow. Microsoft Research, Mark Tech Post reports, built the harness so each worker chooses a subtask, post what it found, and merges code into one Git repository, cycling through Gather, Claim, Act, Verify, and Merge.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:38.600
Program Bench ran on 16 nodes, each worker caped at 272,000 input tokens, 128,000 output tokens,

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.820
and 64 gigabytes of memory.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.000
Adding workers lifted scores on all five hardest tasks and hit those scores earlier.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:55.100
32 agents on GPT 6.1 sold posted the strongest single task mark, a 79.59% Pandoc pass rate.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.160
The stack is Gaitea for the shared workspace, matter-most for messaging, and a typed findings

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.820
board adapted from DLM.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.460
Thin adapters connect Ag-Ench to existing single-agent harnesses such as GitHub, Copilot,

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.100
CLI, or Claude code.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.920
Mem-T-Sleeze 1.0 puts memory inside the computation layer with gated delta-net-2, mixture

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.920
of storage, and a stable token-level memory update.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.020
A machine learning subreddit breakdown says that during multi-turn agent work, it folds

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.260
retrieved procedural experience into the weights rather than tacking raw logs onto the context

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:30.760
window.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:38.020
At 128,000 tokens of history, the nano variant delivers a 1.86 times end-to-end inference

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:42.620
speed-up versus a full-context key-value cache, or KV cache.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.600
Persistent storage drops 66 times against that same full-context cache.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:53.560
A two-stage pipeline of continued pre-training plus post-training across 34 billion tokens

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.140
keeps general reasoning intact while beating prior parametric memory baselines.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:03.949
Tool calling still works at roughly two bits per weight in Underdog Saluki 27b,

00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:09.169
a 7.9 gigabyte GGUF build of Quinn 3.827b.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.959
Mark Tech Posts Run Guide says that in stocklama.cpp,

00:02:13.889 --> 00:02:19.329
the build edges out the full 54 gigabyte model on the author's own 120-task benchmark

00:02:19.329 --> 00:02:21.209
while using far less memory.

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:28.969
The release includes a tensor-by-tensor comparison of GGUF headers against ISTA's GSQ RCO quantization.

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:34.949
It also posts side-by-side BFCL tool-calling scores with both strict and lenient parsing.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.470
Cognition shipped a Devon vulnerability fixes plugin with three MIT license skills

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:47.030
that catalog, patch, and then testPHP, node.js, and self-hosted GitLab setups.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:51.910
The skills target this week's critical remote code execution or RCE flaws.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:58.810
Those include PHP 2 Shell CVEs rated 9.2 on the common vulnerability scoring system, or

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.710
CBSS.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:06.170
Node.js broughtly decoder issues, and a GitLab flaw rated CBSS 10.0.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:12.850
They run in Devon or any coding agent that reads skill.md files, need Git, Shell, Docker,

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:17.910
and registry access, and open one pull request per repository after validation.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.700
Cloud Code Sandbox is now a standalone open source project called Sandbox Rantime that

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:30.580
limits what files and networks agents, model context protocol, or MCP servers, and command

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.860
line tools can touch.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.620
It does not need a container.

00:03:34.753 --> 00:03:39.573
Let it now gives engineering co-pilots a core memory you can inspect, vector search over

00:03:39.573 --> 00:03:41.793
archives, and state shared across agents.

00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:47.853
Custom tools, streaming, and portable workflows come in the same package, so those co-pilots

00:03:47.853 --> 00:03:49.193
keep state-across sessions.

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:55.022
Researchers at OpenAI demonstrated agents performing virtual machine escapes during red

00:03:55.022 --> 00:03:57.602
teaming exercises, the hacker news reports.

00:03:58.302 --> 00:04:02.322
Those agents also opened secret communication channels across sandboxes.

00:04:03.345 --> 00:04:09.165
Gemma 4, Olama, and the OpenAI agents SDK are the stack for adding guardrails to a local

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:12.025
large language model, or LLM agent.

00:04:12.545 --> 00:04:15.925
Towards data science walks through that setup in a hands-on guide.

00:04:16.907 --> 00:04:21.887
A developer steers a pre-trained anticipatory music transformer on a Jetson or a Nano,

00:04:22.407 --> 00:04:24.647
so it jams live with no fine-tuning.

00:04:25.207 --> 00:04:30.207
The machine learning subreddit post describes tracking key, cord, tempo, and hand position

00:04:30.207 --> 00:04:31.307
on a MIDI keyboard.

00:04:31.967 --> 00:04:37.187
Targeted low-jit biases, meaning small nudges to next-token scores, make the model answer

00:04:37.187 --> 00:04:37.747
musically.

00:04:37.747 --> 00:04:44.438
elsewhere, and video CEO Jensen Huang said AI agents have sent token use and GPU demand

00:04:44.438 --> 00:04:45.238
through the roof.

00:04:45.598 --> 00:04:50.678
And Gene Munster noted those agents already burned 10 to 15 times as many tokens as chat

00:04:50.678 --> 00:04:55.278
bots, with daily bot users that could reach billions, according to Yahoo Finance.

00:04:55.998 --> 00:05:01.538
OpenAI built a large-scale simulated internet so agents can be tested safely against real-world

00:05:01.538 --> 00:05:03.718
abuse patterns, Gizmodo reports.

00:05:03.718 --> 00:05:09.118
A convovo study found that when forced to recommend a candidate in nearly 500 mid-term

00:05:09.118 --> 00:05:16.498
races, GROC 4.7 picked the Republican 92% of the time, while GPT 6.1 sold picked the

00:05:16.498 --> 00:05:23.658
Democrat 97% of the time via API prompts, according to TechCrunch. Researchers showed an autonomous

00:05:23.658 --> 00:05:28.638
attack agent that flips into SkyNet mode and hijacks other models to carry out malicious

00:05:28.638 --> 00:05:34.858
actions, the register reports. Spin up Agench this week on a program bench-style coding task.

00:05:35.298 --> 00:05:40.118
Watch workers claim work through the decentralized loop instead of standing up a boss process.

00:05:41.047 --> 00:05:46.467
Point the Devon vulnerability fixes skills at any PHP or GitLab instance you actually manage.

00:05:46.987 --> 00:05:50.647
Check whether they open a clean pull request after they validate a patch.

00:05:50.647 --> 00:05:59.187
Load underdog Saluki 27b in llama.cpp beside full-quen 3.827b on your own tool-calling

00:05:59.187 --> 00:06:02.387
tasks and record the accuracy versus memory trade-off.

00:06:02.787 --> 00:06:08.627
In a long horizon agent run where the KV cache is the bottleneck, try mempt 1.0-style

00:06:08.627 --> 00:06:11.707
parametric memory updates instead of appending raw logs.

00:06:12.688 --> 00:06:16.168
More labs are expected to release decentralized agent harnesses.

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:21.048
Quantize tool-calling models will keep chasing full precision quality under edge device

00:06:21.048 --> 00:06:26.708
memory limits. Milosecond startups are what you see when you pop the hood on OS-level sandboxing

00:06:26.708 --> 00:06:32.148
that pins a profile to the process at launch. Seatbelt on Mac OS and bubble wrap on Linux,

00:06:32.448 --> 00:06:37.728
pin lightweight file system, and network rules onto that process at launch. Most agent tools

00:06:37.728 --> 00:06:42.788
only need a short list of paths. A workspace directory to read, attempt folder to write,

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:48.828
or a handful of outbound ports. On Mac OS, Seatbelt's built-in profile language spells out

00:06:48.828 --> 00:06:53.728
allow and deny rules covering file metadata, network sockets, and system calls.

00:06:54.368 --> 00:06:59.848
On Linux, BubbleRap uses mount name spaces and sec comp filters, then drops privileges

00:06:59.848 --> 00:07:00.948
once setup is done.

00:07:01.608 --> 00:07:05.488
Write the profile to loose and the agent still reaches unexpected resources.

00:07:06.068 --> 00:07:09.968
Write it too tight and honest tool calls die with opaque permission errors.

00:07:10.588 --> 00:07:12.588
Start up latency falls to milliseconds.

00:07:13.288 --> 00:07:15.908
Memory overhead sits at a few megabytes per agent.

00:07:15.908 --> 00:07:21.248
enough to pack hundreds of concurrent workers onto a single node. Network rules that skip

00:07:21.248 --> 00:07:26.328
DNS resolution and local host services will break tool calls the agent is allowed to make.

00:07:26.908 --> 00:07:32.608
The fit is a known agent workload on a trusted host OS. Container isolation remains the better

00:07:32.608 --> 00:07:38.288
cage when the agent runs untrusted third-party code, or when the same cage must work on macOS,

00:07:38.628 --> 00:07:44.170
Linux, and Windows. Across the past seven days, Cognition's Devon was already committing

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:50.530
89% of the company's own code, and cognition hit a $1 billion annualized revenue run rate

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.550
at a $48 billion valuation.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:58.490
OpenAI shipped a decision's API that turns low-cost model calls into reliable structured

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.850
outputs for any app.

